    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nLocated in one of Westport's newest and most sought after developments, 14 Monamore is an energy efficient A-rated, four-bedroom semi-detached residence that comes to the market in exceptional condition having been finished to a very high standard throughout and conveniently situated within walking distance of Westport Town.\n\nWith a floor area of approximately 122sqm/1,313sqft, ground floor accommodation consists of an entrance hall with feature patchwork tilling and a carpeted staircase, a bright living room with herringbone wooden flooring and a large bay window looking onto the green area, an open plan kitchen/dining room with a slide door to the garden, utility room, WC and understair storage.\n \nFirst floor comprises of four bedrooms (master en-suite, two with built in slide robes), bathroom, hotpress and a stira to the attic. uninterrupted Croagh Patrick views are available from the south facing bedrooms. The property is presented in excellent condition having been very well maintained by the current owners, who bought the house from new in 2021.\n\nExternally, there is a cobble lock driveway to the front with space for two cars and side gate entrance for bins etc. The south facing garden to the rear has a small wooden shed in situ (2.8m x 2.2m) and offers uninterrupted Croagh Patrick views. \n\nThis property is likely to appeal to a broad range of buyers, offering fibre broadband for those working remotely and a high yield rental opportunity for someone looking for an investment. Its close proximity to the renowned Great Western Greenway (200m) and all local amenities makes it an attractive option for those seeking a family/holiday/retirement home in one of the west of Irelands most desirable locations\n\nLocation\nMonamore is a prime located on Lodge Road, approximately 1.5km from Westport town, off the main Westport to Castlebar road. It is convenient for all local amenities including primary/secondary schools, shops, restaurants and sports clubs and just 200m from the entrance to the Great Western Greenway. It is also an ideal location for nearby Abbvie Pharmaceuticals and access to Castlebar town. \n\n\nOFFERS IN EXCESS 479,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 6.22m x 2.07m\nFeature tiles, painted and carpeted staircase, understairs storage\n\nLiving Room - 5.45m x 4.02m\nHerringbone wooden floor, bay window, blinds\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 4.5m x 2.98m & 3.31m x 3.27m\nTiled floor, off white Slab kitchen with wood effect formica worktop, glass backsplash, integrated double oven, dishwasher, gas hob, door to garden, Croagh Patrick views\n\nWC - 1.53m x 1.48m\nTile floor, wc, whb unit\n\nUtility Room - 2.4m x 1.76m\nTiled floor, built in storage units, plumbed for washer & dryer.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 3.6m x 1.26m\nCarpeted floor, stira to attic\n\nBedroom One - 4m x 3m\nCarpeted floor, built in sliderobes, blinds, Croagh Patrick Views\n\nBedroom Two - 3.4m x 3.1m & 1.2m x 0.75m\nCarpeted floor, blinds, Croagh Patrick Views\n\nMaster Bedroom - 3.4m x 3.1m & 1.3m x 1m\nCarpeted floor, built in sliderobes, blinds\n\nEn-Suite - 2.2m x 1.2m\nFully tiled, shower, wc, whb unit\n\nBedroom Four - 3m x 2.7m\nCarpeted floor, blinds\n\nBathroom - 3m x 1m & 1.67m x 0.76m\nFully tiled, bath/shower, heated towel rail, wc, whb unit\n\nHotpress - 1.6m x 0.9m\nCarpeted floor, shelving\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Four bedroom semi-detached property located in a sought after residential area</li><li>Completed to an exceptionally high standard having high-quality finishes throughout. </li><li>Gas central heating and solar panels provide an impressive A3 Energy efficient property</li><li>Excellent location within walking distance of Westport town and all its many amenities</li><li>200m from the Great Western Greenway for outdoor enthusiasts and holidaymakers</li><li>Uninterrupted Croagh Patrick views from the enclosed south facing garden and bedrooms</ul>"
      },
